Hi Michael and Emily,

Following Thursday's lab meeting, we'll keep the full received bodies and set=
 aside the rule that cuts everything from the first candidate quote line onwa=
rd. We'll keep the excerpts with the paired readings so we can see what that =
cut took out. The reference labels stay as they are.

In the attached memo, 9 of 86 replies with clear boundaries and 3 of 34 with =
unclear boundaries lost the date of the appointment being moved. Fatima and I=
 checked those 12 replies against the originals on Nov 18. In each excerpt we=
 could still read the request to move the appointment and the requested new d=
ate. The CSV covers all 120 replies we selected from the development partitio=
n. Its eight counts give the four reading outcomes for each boundary group.

Emily, please carry the reading ID and the original boundary rating into the =
next comparison. Let's show the reply count, action changes, and missing orig=
inal appointment dates separately for the clear and unclear groups. Fatima, c=
ould you check the date-loss field against the paired readings before we use =
it for that comparison?

Thanks,
Vanessa

